            {
                "entry_id": "2c4aa7c3-c3c5-31e3-b28d-e9bd5af6ba72",
                "word": "alm",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "32bb3b5d-c6db-4f17-a03e-0256d428fd93",
                        "entry_id": "2c4aa7c3-c3c5-31e3-b28d-e9bd5af6ba72",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "alms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f44202f2-a5b4-3ec6-a3e8-5f3a1bfaf510",
                        "entry_id": "2c4aa7c3-c3c5-31e3-b28d-e9bd5af6ba72",
                        "glosses": [
                            "施捨品"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "nonstandard"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "28d949ba-2d62-495c-a6ef-70327642e10e",
                                "sense_id": "f44202f2-a5b4-3ec6-a3e8-5f3a1bfaf510",
                                "text": "An alm to the poor is a work of charity. Una limosna a los pobres es obra de caridad.",
                                "translation": "向穷人施舍是一种慈善行为。（意思同樣的西班牙語句子）"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31c98d94-c12a-45a9-9588-af2dfbe6043f",
                                "sense_id": "f44202f2-a5b4-3ec6-a3e8-5f3a1bfaf510",
                                "text": "If in doubt, you rarely go wrong giving an alm to the poor, and you might feel better about it.",
                                "translation": "如果有疑问，向穷人施舍很少会错，而且你可能会感觉更好。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0431ca5e-453d-412b-9dbf-d0794ec12a38",
                                "sense_id": "f44202f2-a5b4-3ec6-a3e8-5f3a1bfaf510",
                                "text": "“An alm for the love of God,” cries the beggar. Don Juan stops, reaches in his pocket and holds out his last gold coin above the outstretched arms of the [beggar].",
                                "translation": "“看在上帝的份上，施舍点钱吧。”乞丐喊道。唐璜停下脚步，把手伸进口袋，把最后一枚金币举到乞丐伸出的双臂上方。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b52ca46-cc8d-42ca-bf2b-369724eb5e77",
                                "sense_id": "f44202f2-a5b4-3ec6-a3e8-5f3a1bfaf510",
                                "text": "He wanted to offer it to you, as an alm for the Church, but I told him you would never agree to that. But if you wish to pay one guilder per month, I think he would accept that."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
